  "prompt": "=== Chain-of-thought analysis prompt ===\nYou are a software requirements analyst preparing a UML state machine model.\n\nAnalyze the requirement and extract only the modeling facts needed for a state transition diagram. Keep the analysis concise and evidence-based.\n\nReturn the analysis using exactly these headings:\nStates:\nInitial state:\nFinal states:\nEvents or conditions:\nTransitions:\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n\nDo not write PlantUML in this step.\n\nRequirement:\nAtm Many Scenarios Scenario 7 — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall greet the user when they arrive.\n2. The system shall check the PIN after the card is inserted.\n3. The system shall allow the user to try again if the entered PIN is incorrect.\n4. The system shall keep the card for security if it is invalid or the PIN is entered incorrectly too many times.\n5. The system shall return the card if the user cancels the operation.\n6. The system shall display available options (withdrawing money, checking information, or making a transfer) for the user to choose from if the PIN is correct.\n7. The system shall process the selected request after the user makes a choice.\n\n=== Chain-of-thought analysis response ===\nStates:\nIdle, Greeting, PIN Entry, PIN Incorrect, Options Display, Processing, Card Retained\n\nInitial state:\nIdle\n\nFinal states:\nCard Retained\n\nEvents or conditions:\nCard Inserted, PIN Entered, PIN Correct, PIN Incorrect, Try Again, Cancel, Choice Made\n\nTransitions:\nIdle -> Greeting (Card Inserted)\nGreeting -> PIN Entry (Timer/Default)\nPIN Entry -> PIN Incorrect (PIN Incorrect)\nPIN Entry -> Options Display (PIN Correct)\nPIN Incorrect -> PIN Entry (Try Again)\nPIN Incorrect -> Card Retained (Incorrect PIN Limit Reached)\nOptions Display -> Processing (Choice Made)\nPIN Entry -> Card Retained (Cancel)\nOptions Display -> Card Retained (Cancel)\n\n\n\nMissing or ambiguous details:\n*   Maximum number of incorrect PIN attempts before card retention.\n*   Specific timeout for the Greeting state.\n*   Details of \"Processing\" state - what constitutes completion?\n*   How \"Choice Made\" is signaled (e.g., button press, selection).\n*   What constitutes a \"valid\" card.\n*   Definition of \"available options\" and how they are presented.\n\n=== PlantUML generation prompt ===\nYou are a UML modeling expert.\n\nConvert the requirement and the structured analysis into one UML state transition diagram in PlantUML format.\n\nOutput Rules:\n- Generate ONLY valid PlantUML code.\n- Start with @startuml and end with @enduml.\n- Use [*] for exactly one initial transition.\n- Include at least one final transition to [*].\n- Use clear transition labels when requirement evidence exists.\n- Do not include explanations, analysis, or markdown fences.\n\nRequirement:\nAtm Many Scenarios Scenario 7 — Polished Requirement Specification\n\nFunctional Requirements\n1. The system shall greet the user when they arrive.\n2. The system shall check the PIN after the card is inserted.\n3. The system shall allow the user to try again if the entered PIN is incorrect.\n4. The system shall keep the card for security if it is invalid or the PIN is entered incorrectly too many times.\n5. The system shall return the card if the user cancels the operation.\n6. The system shall display available options (withdrawing money, checking information, or making a transfer) for the user to choose from if the PIN is correct.\n7. The system shall process the selected request after the user makes a choice.\n\nStructured analysis from step 1:\nStates:\nIdle, Greeting, PIN Entry, PIN Incorrect, Options Display, Processing, Card Retained\n\nInitial state:\nIdle\n\nFinal states:\nCard Retained\n\nEvents or conditions:\nCard Inserted, PIN Entered, PIN Correct, PIN Incorrect, Try Again, Cancel, Choice Made\n\nTransitions:\nIdle -> Greeting (Card Inserted)\nGreeting -> PIN Entry (Timer/Default)\nPIN Entry -> PIN Incorrect (PI